    5683	### D44 — Arithmetic topology / Morishita arithmetic Massey products on prime triples (Rédei symbol distribution)
    5684	
    5685	**Question:** Mazur (1966) proposed the analogy "primes in `Spec(Z)`
    5686	↔ knots in `S^3`" and identified the *arithmetic linking number*
    5687	`lk(p, q) := \frac{1 - (p/q)}{2} \in \mathbb{F}_2` (the Legendre
    5688	symbol viewed as a `\mathbb{F}_2`-cocycle on the étale fundamental
    5689	group). Morishita 2002 *Crelle* 550, 141 extended this to higher
    5690	*arithmetic Milnor / Massey products*: the triple Massey product
    5691	`\langle p, q, r \rangle_2 \in \mathbb{F}_2` evaluates to the Rédei
    5692	symbol `[p, q, r]` (Rédei 1939), defined for prime triples with
    5693	all pairwise Legendre symbols `+1` (the "admissible" Borromean
    5694	condition). The Rédei symbol detects whether the triple is
    5695	*Borromean*: pairwise unlinked but jointly linked, like the (13, 61,
    5696	937) example with all Legendre symbols `+1` but Rédei symbol `-1`.
    5697	Question: is the empirical distribution of `[p, q, r]` on admissible
    5698	prime triples below `N` correlated with the Hardy-Littlewood ternary
    5699	singular series prediction `S_3(N)`? If yes, the Rédei symbol gives
    5700	a NEW arithmetic invariant for prime triples — the first cohomological-
    5701	Massey triple-prime invariant, orthogonal to the bilinear-singular-
    5702	series HL framework.
    5703	
    5704	**Why frontier:** the Hardy-Littlewood prime k-tuple conjecture
    5705	predicts the density of prime k-tuples via the singular series
    5706	`S_k = \prod_p (1 - \nu_p / p)^k / (1 - 1/p)^k` — a *bilinear* (pair-
    5707	correlation-via-Möbius) arithmetic invariant. **No project measurement
    5708	has tested whether the singular series captures triple-prime structure
    5709	beyond the bilinear approximation.** The Rédei symbol is the only
    5710	known *arithmetic-cohomological* triple invariant on prime triples
