    ## Key Papers Found:
    
    1. **"Noncommutative geometry and motives: the thermodynamics of endomotives"** (arXiv:math/0512138)
       - Authors: Alain Connes, Caterina Consani, Matilde Marcolli
       - Semigroups of endomorphisms of algebraic varieties give rise canonically to such endomotives, with an action of the absolute Galois group. The semigroup of endomorphisms of the multiplicative group yields the Bost-Connes system, from which one obtains, through the above procedure, the desired cohomological interpretation of the zeros of the Riemann zeta function.
    
    2. **"KMS states and complex multiplication"** (arXiv:math/0501424)
       - Authors: Alain Connes, Matilde Marcolli, Niranjan Ramachandran
       - This system admits the Dedekind zeta function as partition function and the Idele class group as group of symmetries. The extremal KMS states at zero temperature intertwine this symmetry with the Galois action on the values of the states on the arithmetic subalgebra.
    
    3. **"Fun with F₁"** (arXiv:0806.2401)
       - The algebra and the endomotive of the quantum statistical mechanical system of Bost--Connes naturally arises by extension of scalars from the "field with one element" to rational numbers. The inductive structure of the abelian part of the endomotive corresponds to the tower of finite extensions of that "field", while the endomorphisms reflect the Frobenius correspondences.
    
    These papers explore the deep connections between the Bost-Connes quantum statistical mechanical system, endomotives, KMS phase transitions, and Galois theory.
    
    
